all right so good number of people in  our office tried to get into middle gear  survive and play their Salvage missions  and found it pretty confusing the game  has a pretty complicated crafting system  upfront and the staging area can be a  bit convoluted so we're gonna take you  through some tips to get you through  your first couple of rounds and some  pretty cool ways to set up traps and  defend your base so before you start the  first thing you should know is that you  can't invert your controls from the  staging area only the main menu that one  took me way too long to figure out so if  you play inverted do it after the  customization section but before you  start the game once you get to the  starting area you'll find yourself in a  sterile environment it's really not too  bad there's two main stations you need  to go to first head over to the supply  box where the game will give you rewards  blueprints and materials pretty much go  the supply box after every round or when  you log in and check it for material you  can then take that over to the  customization area where you pretty much  craft everything there's a menu where  you can actually go and give yourself a  couple more item slots and I recommend  doing it in general having a mixed  loadouts pretty important you aren't  good crowd control such as shotguns  range weapons such as assault rifles hit  the legs of exploding enemies and a  trusted melee weapon now the game  doesn't actually start you off with a  lot of material so what I recommend is  actually going into a couple of solo  Salvage missions and completely ignoring  the wormhole generator what I found is  if you walk around and just collect  material even if you fail you get to  take it with you back to your starting  area so consider failing a couple times  building up your resources and using  that to go to the crafting stations and  crafting your first set of good gear  fences and traps all right so you're  ready to do your first salvage mission  you have to go to the accept mission  area and neither accept quick match  which will start on the matchmaking  lobby or pull your friends in but either  way you have to both select the mission  and then walk over to another deployment  circle to start the mission craft as  much ammo and as many barricades as you  can before matchmaking because you only  have about five minutes once you get  into the round to get to the area that  you have to defend and also you won't  pick up much on the way there that's  gonna help you build anything you may  find yourself getting wounded by the  first set of zombies on your way there  there's a couple different types of  damage there's general damage which you  can use a spray to get rid of and  they're specific damage which you need  to go into the menu to heal you'll know  if you have a specific damage on your  body because you'll see continuous  bleeding on screen on the easier salvage  missions you can probably ignore  specific damage because the round will  be over before  becomes a problem the other thing you're  on the lookout for our coupon crystals  they look like little plants and you can  use those points to level up characters  or throw them to attract zombies now  once you get to the defense area the  biggest noob mistake we're seeing right  now is people placing their traps and  barricades inside of the red circle but  what you have to do is build outside of  that red circle because the warp gate  will actually destroy your gear  barricades between waves in your  inventory you'll also find a warp point  this is not for kidnapping creatures  it's actually something you can put  anywhere on the map and teleport to so  put it somewhere safe like up high and  then if you get in trouble you can warp  yourself to safety now you'll see the  zombie pass right away it varies  depending on the map but the zombies  really do stick to these arrows you can  go ahead and start deploying fences  along those lines and as long as you  stay behind the fences the zombies will  pile up on them  the zombies won't actually go around the  fences unless there's a player standing  right next to one and a zombie lunges  sideways hi bear kids or low barricades  are both equally as good they slow down  zombies and let you attack through them  if you look through the menu each one  will say what kind of melee attacks are  compatible at this point you can start  experimenting with fun trap combos we  like putting a propeller in front or  behind a fence if it's in front of the  fence then the zombies will get ground  up as they go into the fence if it's  behind the fence the zombies all topple  over at the same time and get ground up  after they fall  another neat combo is to toss crystals  at a horde of zombies which they'll all  bunch up around and then follow up with  a grenade now after a couple of rounds  you can actually go find a walker so if  you see people running around with those  they found them on the map and they're  pretty much a guaranteed win at the  easier levels all right so let's say you  made it to the end of the round there's  some things you should do to conserve  your resources such as if the countdown  timer says 10 seconds left and the  zombies aren't anywhere close to the  warp gate conserve your ammo because you  have to craft everything in this game  you can also trash and disassemble  barricades up in to the point where the  round ends we're not quite sure that  returns the material to you or not  but you have a limited amount of time to  do it all right so you made it through  the match what should you be doing back  in your staging area well depending on  how well you did you can use points to  toughen up and maintain your gear you  can put points into toughening your  character and individual skills like  heavy attacks or punching kicking and  tripping enemies and you can craft extra  material and send that to your  repository which is a storage box that  you can get to in the next round alright  that sugar you guys started on Metal  Gear survived salvage mission we'd love  to hear about your creative traps and  tactics so let us know in the comments  below don't forget to keep an eye on  gamespot.com as we cover more Metal Gear  survived up until launch  [Music]
 

